28. Climbing Stairs — LeetCode #70

Pattern: Dynamic Programming

class Solution {
    public int climbStairs(int n) {

        int one = 1;
        int two = 1;

        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {

            int current = one + two;

            two = one;
            one = current;
        }

        return one;
    }
}

Example:

Input: 5
Output: 8
Logic

You can climb either:

1 step
or
2 steps

So:

ways(n) = ways(n - 1) + ways(n - 2)

This is basically the Fibonacci pattern.

Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)

29. Linked List Cycle — LeetCode #141

Pattern: Fast & Slow Pointers

public class Solution {
    public boolean hasCycle(ListNode head) {

        ListNode slow = head;
        ListNode fast = head;

        while (fast != null && fast.next != null) {

            slow = slow.next;
            fast = fast.next.next;

            if (slow == fast) {
                return true;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }
}
🧠 Core idea

Two runners:

slow → 1 step
fast → 2 steps

If there is a cycle:

slow ↘
       → → →
fast ↗

Eventually they meet.

If no cycle → fast reaches null.

Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)

30. Binary Tree Level Order Traversal — LeetCode #102

Pattern: BFS + Queue

class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> levelOrder(TreeNode root) {

        List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();

        if (root == null) {
            return result;
        }

        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new LinkedList<>();

        queue.add(root);

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {

            int size = queue.size();

            List<Integer> level = new ArrayList<>();

            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {

                TreeNode current = queue.poll();

                level.add(current.val);

                if (current.left != null) {
                    queue.add(current.left);
                }

                if (current.right != null) {
                    queue.add(current.right);
                }
            }

            result.add(level);
        }

        return result;
    }
}

